{"book":10,"chapter":12,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / RUST AFTER PYTHON / CHAPTER 12","slides":[{"title":"list and Vec","sub":"Chapter 12 · Python → Rust","short":"Intro","main":"What matches a list; traps that vanish.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["list","Operations","Traps"],"captions":["The list is Python's main structure; Rust has Vec, arrays and slices","Add, remove, slices, copying, sorting, comprehensions, queues","Traps: changing while iterating, shared refs, “list of lists” — gone or caught at build time in Rust"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"list","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Vec / [T; N] / &[T]","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":36.0,"y":66.0,"w":64.0,"h":28.0,"text":"push","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":108.0,"y":66.0,"w":64.0,"h":28.0,"text":"slices","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":64.0,"h":28.0,"text":"copies","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":252.0,"y":66.0,"w":64.0,"h":28.0,"text":"sort","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a4","x":324.0,"y":66.0,"w":64.0,"h":28.0,"text":"queue","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":250.0,"h":34.0,"text":"errors at build time, not at run time","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[16.9,29.7]}]},{"title":"Homogeneity","sub":"Element types","short":"Homogeneity","main":"Vec is homogeneous; different types: enum.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["list","Vec and array","enum"],"captions":["Python list: [1, \"a\", [2]] — any types in a row","Vec<T> and [T; N]: one element type; a tuple mixes types but has fixed length","Different types in a vector: use an enum, each variant holds its own data"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":90.0,"y":66.0,"w":62.0,"h":32.0,"text":"1","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":162.0,"y":66.0,"w":62.0,"h":32.0,"text":"\"a\"","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":234.0,"y":66.0,"w":62.0,"h":32.0,"text":"[2]","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":90.0,"y":50.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"1","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":146.0,"y":50.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"2","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":202.0,"y":50.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"3","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":106.0,"w":160.0,"h":28.0,"text":"(1, \"a\", 2.5) — tuple","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["enum Val { Int(i32), Text(String) }","let v: Vec<Val> = vec![…];"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.9,25.9]}]},{"title":"Core methods","sub":"push, pop, remove","short":"Methods","main":"append → push; pop returns Option; remove by value: retain.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["append → push","pop → Option","remove and in"],"captions":["append → push; extend → extend; insert → insert; len → len; clear → clear","pop() → pop() returns Option: an empty vector has no last; pop(i) → remove(i)","x in l → contains(&x); l.remove(x) by value → retain or position + remove"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["l.append(x)   →   v.push(x)","l.extend(m)   →   v.extend(m)","l.insert(i, x) →  v.insert(i, x)"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["l.pop()    →   v.pop()      // Option","l.pop(i)   →   v.remove(i)"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["x in l       →   v.contains(&x)","l.remove(x)  →   v.retain(|&e| e != x)"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.1,22.3]}]},{"title":"Indexes and slices","sub":"No negative indexes","short":"Slices","main":"last(); a slice is a reference; step_by, chunks, windows.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["l[-1]","A slice is a reference","Step and windows"],"captions":["No negative indexes: v.last() or v[v.len() - 1]","Python slice is a copy; Rust &v[a..b] is a reference to part, no copying","l[::2] → v.iter().step_by(2); chunks(n) cuts into pieces, windows(n) gives sliding windows"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"l[-1]","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"v.last()","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"l[1:3] — a copy","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"&v[1..3] — a reference","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["v.iter().step_by(2)","v.chunks(3)      // [1,2,3] [4,5,6]","v.windows(2)     // [1,2] [2,3] [3,4]"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[15.0,25.1]}]},{"title":"Copying","sub":"Aliases and clones","short":"Copying","main":"Move, clone, to_vec.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Python: alias","Rust: move","clone and to_vec"],"captions":["l2 = l — one value under two names; copy(), nested: deepcopy()","let b = a; moves the vector: the old variable is unusable — no accidental sharing","a.clone() — a deep copy; s.to_vec() — a vector from a slice"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":60.0,"y":70.0,"w":50.0,"h":36.0,"text":"l\n→","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":60.0,"y":118.0,"w":50.0,"h":36.0,"text":"l2\n→","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":86.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":220.0,"y2":90.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":86.0,"y1":118.0,"x2":220.0,"y2":100.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":270.0,"y":94.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"[1, 2]","tone":"muted","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let a = vec![1, 2];","let b = a;     // moved","// a is unavailable"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let b = a.clone();      // deep copy","let c = a[1..].to_vec();"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.2,22.9]}]},{"title":"Changing while iterating","sub":"Build error","short":"Iteration","main":"retain, drain, filter + collect.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Python","Rust: build error","retain and drain"],"captions":["Python: removing from a list inside a loop over it skips items — bug only on some data","Rust: the loop holds a reference to the vector — no mutation at the same time; build error","Right way: retain (by condition, one pass), drain (pull a range), filter + collect"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["for x in l:","    if x < 0: l.remove(x)   # skips"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["for x in &v {","    v.remove(0);   // ✕ cannot borrow","}"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["v.retain(|&x| x >= 0);","let d: Vec<i32> = v.drain(1..3).collect();"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.6,28.6]}]},{"title":"Sorting","sub":"sort, key, bisect","short":"Sorting","main":"sort, sort_by_key, binary_search, max, min.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["sort","key","bisect"],"captions":["sorted(l) → copy + sort(); l.sort() → v.sort() in place; for f64: sort_by and partial_cmp","key=… → sort_by_key; reverse=True → sort_by with reversed comparison","max, min — Option; sum — a number; bisect → binary_search: Ok(pos) or Err(insert point)"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["v.sort();","w.sort_by(|a, b| a.partial_cmp(b).unwrap());"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["v.sort_by_key(|s| s.len());","v.sort_by(|a, b| b.cmp(a));   // descending"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["v.binary_search(&5)   // Ok(2) or Err(2)","v.iter().max()       // Option"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.5,25.3]}]},{"title":"Comprehensions","sub":"Iterators","short":"Comprehensions","main":"filter + map + collect; zip, enumerate, windows, fold.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Comprehension","zip and enumerate","Laziness"],"captions":["[f(x) for x in l if c(x)] → v.iter().filter(c).map(f).collect()","zip glues sequences, enumerate adds indexes, windows compares neighbors","Until collect, sum or for, nothing is computed; fold builds any result"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["v.iter()","    .filter(|x| **x > 0)","    .map(|x| x * 2)","    .collect::<Vec<_>>()"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["a.iter().zip(b.iter())","v.iter().enumerate()","v.windows(2).all(|w| w[0] <= w[1])"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let s = v.iter().fold(0, |acc, x| acc + x);","let it = v.iter().map(|x| x + 1);  // computes nothing"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":8.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.3,24.1]}]},{"title":"Capacity","sub":"capacity","short":"Capacity","main":"len and capacity; doubling; with_capacity.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["len and capacity","Growth ×2","with_capacity"],"captions":["len is how many elements; capacity is how many fit without a new allocation","When capacity runs out, the vector allocates twice as much and copies the data — like a Python list","Vec::with_capacity(1000) and reserve(n) allocate once; shrink_to_fit gives back the excess"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":56.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"1","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":106.0,"y":56.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"2","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":162.0,"y":56.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"3","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b0","x":218.0,"y":56.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"","tone":"muted","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b1","x":274.0,"y":56.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"","tone":"muted","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"len = 3, capacity = 5","size":10.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":100.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":34.0,"text":"cap 4 → full","tone":"yellow","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":168.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":212.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"cap 8 + copy","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let mut v = Vec::with_capacity(1000);","v.reserve(500);"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.8,26.9]}]},{"title":"Different types","sub":"enum and dyn Trait","short":"Mixed types","main":"A closed and an open set of types.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["enum","Box<dyn Trait>","Choice"],"captions":["Vector of enums: all variants known, match handles each","Vector of Box<dyn Trait>: any struct with the trait — for extensible systems","Fixed set — enum; open set — trait objects (covered in the traits chapter)"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let v = vec![Shape::Circle(1.0), Shape::Rect(2.0, 3.0)];"],"lang":"rust","size":8.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let v: Vec<Box<dyn Plugin>> = vec![","    Box::new(A), Box::new(B),","];"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"enum\nclosed set","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"dyn Trait\nopen set","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[14.6,28.3]}]},{"title":"Stack and queue","sub":"Vec, VecDeque, BinaryHeap","short":"Queues","main":"Vec — stack, VecDeque — queue, BinaryHeap — heap.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Stack","VecDeque","BinaryHeap"],"captions":["Vec is a stack: push and pop at the end in constant time","Queue: Python deque → VecDeque; insert/remove at the front of a Vec is linear — unsuitable","heapq → BinaryHeap: fast maximum; all in the standard library"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":90.0,"y":66.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"1","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":146.0,"y":66.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"2","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":202.0,"y":66.0,"w":48.0,"h":32.0,"text":"3","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":290.0,"y":66.0,"w":50.0,"h":32.0,"text":"push/pop","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"push_back\npop_front","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"VecDeque","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"heapq","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"BinaryHeap","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.7,28.9]}]},{"title":"Two-dimensional lists","sub":"The [[0]*n]*m trap","short":"Grids","main":"vec![vec![0; n]; m]; a flat vector.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Python trap","vec![vec![…]]","Flat vector"],"captions":["[[0] * n] * m — all rows are one list: changing one changes all","vec![vec![0; n]; m] clones the inner vector per row: rows are independent","For speed — one flat Vec and the index row * width + col"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"r0","x":60.0,"y":40.0,"w":70.0,"h":22.0,"text":"→","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r1","x":60.0,"y":68.0,"w":70.0,"h":22.0,"text":"→","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r2","x":60.0,"y":96.0,"w":70.0,"h":22.0,"text":"→","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":270.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"[0, 0, 0]","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let mut g = vec![vec![0; 3]; 2];","g[0][1] = 5;   // only the first row"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let w = 3;","let mut a = vec![0; w * 2];","a[row * w + col] = 5;"],"hl":[2],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.1,30.8]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What next","short":"Recap","main":"Next: classes, traits, operators.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Remember","Cheat sheet","Next"],"captions":["Vec is homogeneous, slices are refs, copying is explicit, mutation while iterating: retain and drain","Mixed types: enum or dyn Trait; queue: VecDeque; heap: BinaryHeap; grid: vec![vec![…]]","Next chapter: classes, traits and operator overloading"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Vec","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"&[T]","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"clone","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"retain","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let mut v = vec![3, 1, 2];","v.sort(); v.retain(|&x| x > 1);"],"lang":"rust","size":11.